  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Decision\\n\\nThe integration should expect **`InvalidCursorError`, code `INVALID_CURSOR`** — a fail‑closed rejection — not a generic ledger failure and not a silent restart of the feed.\\n\\n## Why\\n\\n**1. The “stored observation cursor” is Ordarium’s ORD‑BOOT‑0 state‑change feed cursor.**\\nIn the pinned `@ordarium/core` contract it is `StateChangePage.cursor`: the durable, filter‑independent position of the last delivered committed state revision. Unlike the optional `nextCursor` of the other read surfaces it is *always* present precisely so a consumer can persist it, reach the end of the feed, and resume later when new revisions commit (`types.d.ts`, `StateChangeFeed`, `StateStore.changes`). “Rejected” therefore means the stored position cannot be accepted as a durable resume point.\\n\\n**2. The pinned Ordarium line supplies a dedicated error for exactly that case.**\\nThe operative basis is ordarium **1.3.1**, consistent across `package.json`, the `pnpm-workspace.yaml` overrides, and the installed artifacts (`node_modules/@ordarium/core` 1.3.1, `@ordarium/ledger-sqlite` 1.3.1). In that artifact:\\n\\n- `errors.js` defines `InvalidCursorError` → code `INVALID_CURSOR`, message *“The c",
